{"id": "y0515", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, considering the options, a pocket is definitely the most practical choice for carrying a book while traveling. A backpack or suitcase would work too, but they' re not as convenient as having it right at hand. The other options like the Library of Congress or syn agogue aren't really meant for personal storage during travel. So yeah, a pocket is the best answer here.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0523", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Getting in shape typically requires a combination of exercise, good health habits, and consistent effort. So while all the options listed are related to fitness, the most essential factor is exercise. Regular physical activity helps build muscle tone, improve cardiovascular health, and increase overall well-being. However, without good health practices like proper nutrition or adequate rest, even intense exercise may not lead to sustainable results. Swe ating and feeling better can be side effects of working out but aren't the primary drivers. So the best answer would be B: exercise, as it's the foundational element for getting in shape.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 32, "carrier_ended": null}
