{"id": "y0555", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 18, "onset_chunk": 17, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The best example of water being an electrical conduct or would be A, lightning hitting water and organisms inside dying. When lightning strike s water, it passes through the water because water conducts electricity, which can cause harm to anything in its path, including living things.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0563", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Photosynthesis can be performed by a cabbage cell . Cabbage cells contain chlorophyll, which allows them to carry out photos ynthesis. Be e cells and bear cells do not perform photosynthesis as they are animal cells without chloro phyll. Cat cells also lack chloro phyll, so they cannot perform photosynthesis.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 17, "carrier_ended": null}
